---
import CsvImportPreview from '../components/CsvImportPreview.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Import your history"
  description="Preview and validate an escape-room spreadsheet before importing it into Escape Atlas."
>
  <header class="page-header import-page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Bring your history</p>
    <h1>Your spreadsheet is not the problem. Being trapped inside it is.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Escape Atlas turns a CSV into a clean, portable room history. Everything runs locally in the browser: inspect every normalized row, fix any errors, then download the valid result.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="import-principles" aria-label="Import process">
    <article><span>01</span><h3>Choose a CSV</h3><p>Use the template or bring a spreadsheet with familiar headings such as Room, Operator, Town and Played Date.</p></article>
    <article><span>02</span><h3>Review the dry run</h3><p>Dates, times, outcomes and defaults are normalized. Errors stay attached to the exact source row.</p></article>
    <article><span>03</span><h3>Keep the clean copy</h3><p>Download the valid rows in a stable column order. The source file never leaves your device.</p></article>
  </section>

  <CsvImportPreview />

  <section class="section import-boundary" aria-labelledby="import-boundary-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Deliberate boundary</p>
      <h2 id="import-boundary-heading">A useful static tool, not a half-built account system.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>This site remains Anthony and Trenna's public archive and planning companion. Any future multi-user product will be designed as a separate application rather than grafted onto this Cloudflare Pages site.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
